  "about": "How the synthetic voice says what the panels write (tools/voice/narrate.mjs). The panels keep their text; this only changes what is spoken. units: after a number ('511 keV'); words: whole words, case as written; symbols: anywhere; patterns: regular expressions ($1 for a group). A story's own entries (stories.<key>) come before the global ones, the longest first. The voice is American (en-us), so units are spelled the American way here; the text on screen stays British. Check new entries with node tools/voice/narrate.mjs <key> --phonemes.",
